0011: # In the input you will see a grid with several colored pixels at the top.
0012: # To make the output, you should draw a pattern downward from each pixel:
0013: # Color the diagonal corners, and then color downward with a vertical period of 2 from those corners and from the original pixel, making the pattern fall downward.
0014: 
0015: def main(input_grid):
0016:     """
0017:     Grow a downward period-2 pixel pattern from each colored seed pixel.
0018: 
0019:     Input structure:
0020:     - The grid has a black background.
0021:     - One or more isolated colored pixels act as seeds.
0022:     - Seed colors are distinct and remain the colors of their generated patterns.
0023: 
0024:     Rule:
0025:     - Detect all single-pixel colored components.
0026:     - From each seed, start trails at the seed and its four diagonal neighboring positions.
0027:     - Continue each trail downward every two rows while it remains inside the grid.
0028: 
0029:     Key insight:
0030:     - Each seed generates a sparse falling pattern from five starting offsets, preserving its color.
0031:     """
0032:     # Plan:
0033:     # 1. Find the pixels and make the output
0034:     # 2. Grow the pixel pattern downward from each pixel
0035: 
0036:     # Extract the pixels (single-cell monochromatic components)
